      "problem": "$\\int v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\\,\\,=\\,$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         $+\\text{ }C$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that \n\n$$\n\\int {csc}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t=-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t+C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int 3{csc}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t & =3\\int {csc}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3(-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t)+C \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{cot}⁡t+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
